PROPOSAL — NOT APPLIED. This is the minimal "drop the legacy row" change a
persistent-shell preset needs before a realm can declare the confined terminal
face. It is a diff against `tests/kits/_shared/preset-seam.mjs` (OUR file, the
one shape 19 kit/world assemblies mount), NOT against a pinned-host bundle.

WHY IT IS NOT APPLIED HERE: it changes what 19 kits assert about the Member's
shell (persistent state, PTY identity, `/dev/pts/N`) and none of those kits is
the thing being decided. It is shown so the cost is visible, not to ship it.

THE FAILURE IT PREVENTS (measured, not argued): if a preset keeps this group
and the realm declares `terminal`, `installMemberIoProviders` throws
`TERMINALS_DOUBLE_TERMINAL_REFUSED`
(`packages/runtime/team-services/src/install.ts#L375-L386`) before any Member
scope exists, and `agent-bindings.mjs` fails closed on a mount rejection — the
Member is rolled back, not created with a missing shell. Pinned by
`tests/world-factory/a5sf-pd13-terminal-read-axis.test.mjs` arm C4.

--- a/tests/kits/_shared/preset-seam.mjs
+++ b/tests/kits/_shared/preset-seam.mjs
@@ -98,21 +98,17 @@
 export function persistentShellGroup({ timeoutMs = 300_000, bashDescription } = {}) {
   return {
-    id: 'persistent-shell',
-    name: 'cordis:group',
-    group: true,
-    isolate: { terminals: true },
-    config: [
-      { id: 'pty', name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-terminal' },
-      { id: 'terminal-bash', name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-terminal-bash', config: { timeoutMs } },
-      {
-        id: 'persistent-bash',
-        name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-bash-persistent',
-        config: {
-          timeoutMs,
-          ...(bashDescription !== undefined ? { description: bashDescription } : {}),
-        },
-      },
-    ],
+    // The old group is REPLACED, not supplemented: one `bash` name, served by
+    // the transient host tool until the realm's route-C shadow re-registers it
+    // on the confined terminal face. Keeping `pty`/`terminal-bash` here leaves a
+    // live ancestor `terminals` service and the realm install refuses.
+    id: 'tool-bash',
+    name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-bash',
+    ...(bashDescription === undefined ? {} : { config: { description: bashDescription } }),
   }
 }
@@
 export function smokePresetPlugins({ personaText, cwdSuffix, bashTimeoutMs, bashDescription }) {
@@
-    persistentShellGroup({ ...(bashTimeoutMs !== undefined ? { timeoutMs: bashTimeoutMs } : {}), ...(bashDescription !== undefined ? { description: bashDescription } : {}) }),
+    persistentShellGroup({ ...(bashTimeoutMs !== undefined ? { timeoutMs: bashTimeoutMs } : {}), ...(bashDescription !== undefined ? { description: bashDescription } : {}) }),

WHAT THIS COSTS (user-visible, per kit world):
  - `cd`/`export` no longer survive a `bash` call; a second call starts in the
    session cwd. Kits that assert a persisted cwd (`u6-*`, `u7-tbash-*`,
    `a5-w7-*`) would need the `workdir` argument instead.
  - no interactive stdin; a kit that sends a command and then types into the
    same shell has nothing to type into.
  - no `/dev/pts/N` identity to observe: `a5sf-pty-contract.test.mjs` and
    `lib/a5sf-pty-contract-world.mjs` inject a real `TerminalSessionService`
    port, so they keep working — but a world that asserts the Member's shell is
    a PTY would assert something that is no longer true.
  - `run_in_background`: the transient tool HAS it, the confined terminal tool
    does not — so this direction keeps jobs and gains the read axis; the
    governed preset still ends up without it after the shadow.

FOR A PINNED-HOST PRESET (`minimal.patch.yml`) THE SAME EDIT IS FORBIDDEN:
`CORE PATCH BUDGET = 0` — that file is upstream's and is never patched. An
operator who wants the governed shell selects a preset like
`exemplar/governed-member-preset.patch.yml` instead of editing the host bundle.
